# The certification harness writes this into apps/desktop after a run. It records the AWS
# account the run happened in — and this repository is going public, so it must never be
# committed. The naming-law scan would fail the build if it were (it walks .json too), but a
# guard that fires is a worse outcome than a file that was never staged.
leaves-no-trace.cert.json
